					</textElement>
					<textFieldExpression><![CDATA[($F{entityName1}==null?"":$F{entityName1})+ "<br />" +
($F{mailingAddress1}==null?"":$F{mailingAddress1})+($F{mailingCity}==null?"":$F{mailingCity})+", "+
($F{mailingState}==null?"":$F{mailingState})+" " + ($F{mailingPostal}==null?"":$F{mailingPostal})+ "<br />"]]></textFieldExpression>
				</textField>
				<textField textAdjust="StretchHeight">
					<reportElement x="0" y="81" width="572" height="329" uuid="95d0e317-8ea0-48bb-ba9e-992431a4ad6e">
						<property name="com.jaspersoft.studio.unit.height" value="px"/>
					</reportElement>
					<box topPadding="2" leftPadding="10" bottomPadding="2" rightPadding="10"/>
					<textElement textAlignment="Justified" verticalAlignment="Top" markup="html">
						<font fontName="Arial" size="12"/>
						<paragraph lineSpacing="Single"/>
					</textElement>
					<textFieldExpression><![CDATA["Dear Customer,<br /><br />"+

"This month is your <b>settle up month</b> for Budget Billing.  The last bill that you received reflects the actual charges for services plus or minus your current deferred balance.  Please pay the amount shown on your last bill statement.  Next month, we will begin billing your new budget amount.  As in the beginning, we have averaged your bills from the most recent twelve months history to determine your new budget amount.  Your budget amount is a suggested amount, based on your usage, to help ensure a minimal settle up bill.  Your next eleven bills will be designated <b>Budget Bills</b> and will reflect the new budget amount of $"+ $F{CMSBUDAM}.setScale(2) + " along with showing the actual charges for the month.  The twelfth bill will again be a settle up bill for the next twelve months.<br /><br />"+

"As I mentioned before, by signing up for budget, you are agreeing to always pay the budget amount each month regardless of the actual bill amount.  You also understand that some months your budget amount will be more than the actual charges and some months it will be less than your actual charges.  Budget will only work if you pay the agreed upon budgeted amount each month.  If you notice, on your utility bill, that your budget deferred balance is underpaid this means you are not paying enough every month and you should consider contacting us to increase your budget bill amount.<br /><br />"+

"If you have any questions or concerns, please contact a customer service representative at (979) 764-3535.<br /><br />"+

"Sincerely, <br /><br /><br/>"+

"Customer Service Representative<br /><br />"]]></textFieldExpression>
				</textField>
				<textField textAdjust="StretchHeight" isBlankWhenNull="true">
					<reportElement stretchType="RelativeToBandHeight" x="0" y="25" width="572" height="25" isPrintWhenDetailOverflows="true" uuid="d71d9aad-922f-47b3-88f6-92e414be2c6d">
						<property name="com.jaspersoft.studio.unit.x" value="px"/>
						<property name="com.jaspersoft.studio.unit.height" value="px"/>
						<property name="com.jaspersoft.studio.unit.y" value="px"/>
					</reportElement>
					<box topPadding="5" leftPadding="10" rightPadding="10"/>
